## Infrastructure as Code (AWS CDK)

### Stack Structure

```
infrastructure/
├── bin/
│   └── expense-app.ts          # CDK app entry point
├── lib/
│   ├── stacks/
│   │   ├── staging-stack.ts   # Main staging stack
│   │   ├── database-stack.ts  # RDS PostgreSQL (minimal)
│   │   ├── storage-stack.ts    # S3 bucket (minimal)
│   │   ├── email-stack.ts      # SES configuration
│   │   └── compute-stack.ts    # Lambda + API Gateway
│   └── constructs/
│       ├── nextjs-lambda.ts   # Next.js Lambda deployment
│       ├── api-gateway.ts      # API Gateway setup
│       └── rds-instance.ts     # RDS instance (minimal)
└── config/
    └── staging.json            # Staging-specific config
```

### CDK Configuration Rules

**Staging Stack (`staging-stack.ts`):**
```typescript
// CRITICAL: All resources must use minimal configurations
const stagingConfig = {
  rds: {
    instanceClass: 'db.t3.micro',  // Smallest available
    allocatedStorage: 20,          // Minimum GB
    multiAz: false,                // Single AZ only
    backupRetentionDays: 7,        // Minimum
  },
  lambda: {
    memorySize: 128,               // Minimum MB
    timeout: 30,                   // Seconds
    reservedConcurrentExecutions: undefined, // No reservation
  },
  s3: {
    versioning: false,             // Disabled
    lifecycleRules: [],            // None
  },
};
```

**Environment Variables:**
- Use AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store for secrets
- Use environment variables for non-sensitive config
- Never hardcode credentials or secrets

